 # Plenoxels Training Configuration (PeRFception variants)
+
 Also called: PeRFception-CO3D training, PeRFception-ScanNet training
 
 ## Overview
-This configuration defines the specific hyperparameters, initialization strategies, and training schedules for optimizing Plenoxels on the CO3D and ScanNet datasets, as introduced in the PeRFception framework. It addresses the instability of standard Plenoxels training on object-centric (CO3D) and indoor (ScanNet) data by adjusting learning rates, loss weights, and voxel pruning thresholds. It differs from the baseline [Plenoxels Training](5979-plenoxels-training.md) by employing a 10× higher sparsity loss lambda, disabling background rendering for ScanNet, and using depth-map-based initialization for ScanNet to mitigate floaters.
+This configuration defines the specific hyperparameters, initialization strategies, and training schedules required to optimize Plenoxels for the CO3D and ScanNet datasets, as implemented in the PeRFception framework [S1]. It addresses dataset-specific challenges such as sparse observation, motion blur, and background ambiguity by modifying learning rates, loss weights, and voxel initialization methods [S1]. It differs from standard Plenoxels configurations by employing distinct initialization pipelines for ScanNet (depth-based) versus CO3D (default), disabling background rendering for indoor scenes, and applying a sparsity loss ten times stronger than the default [S1].
 
 ## How it works
+The method optimizes voxel opacity ($\sigma$) and spherical harmonic (SH) coefficients using gradient-based optimization. The implementation relies on the official Plenoxels PyTorch implementation with custom CUDA kernels [S1].
+
